<section class="section rule-top">
<div class="wrap stack-v">
<h2>Why Freeland</h2>
<p class="lede">Five things you can check before you book.</p>
<ul class="rows">
<li>
<h3>You talk to Kevin.</h3>
<p>Kevin reads your numbers and makes the calls himself. There is no account manager between you and the person accountable for the work.</p>
<p><a href="/results/#client-reviews">Read Sasha Gooray’s review</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>One plan, from ad to reorder.</h3>
<p>The ad, the offer, the page and the follow-up are read together and fixed in order. A cheaper click helps little if the page or the follow-up loses the buyer.</p>
<p><a href="/results/">See the track record</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>Store sales, not platform claims.</h3>
<p>An ad platform's reported return is one input, not a profit statement. Calls are checked against what your store actually sold.</p>
<p><a href="/services/meta-ads/">How we read Meta ads</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>Repeat work with checks.</h3>
<p>Daily ad checks, scheduled sale changes and weekly reports run on a system that keeps a record of what it did. When something needs judgment, a person looks at it.</p>
<p><a href="/how-it-works/">What the system does</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<h3>Built for supplement ad limits.</h3>
<p>Each supplement brand gets a list of what it can and cannot say, and copy is checked against it before it runs. Page prices are checked against the real checkout before ad money is spent. Final claim approval stays with you.</p>
<p><a href="/for/supplement-brands/">How we work with supplement brands</a></p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
